### Sample requests. Works with the "REST Client" extension in VS Code or IntelliJ's HTTP client.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Create an expense
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Lunch at canteen",
  "amount": 250.50,
  "category": "Food",
  "date": "2026-10-20",
  "description": "Thali and lassi"
}

### 2. List all expenses
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/expenses

### 3. Get one expense
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/expenses/1

### 4. Update an expense
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/expenses/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Dinner with family",
  "amount": 900.00,
  "category": "Food",
  "date": "2026-10-21",
  "description": "Updated entry"
}

### 5. Filter by date range
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/expenses/filter?start=2026-10-01&end=2026-10-31

### 6. Filter by date range + category
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/expenses/filter?start=2026-10-01&end=2026-10-31&category=Food

### 7. Summary
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/expenses/summary?start=2026-10-01&end=2026-10-31

### 8. Delete
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/expenses/1

### 9. Validation error demo (expects 400 with fieldErrors)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "", "amount": -10, "category": "", "date": "2099-01-01" }
